pyiceberg-core itself is licensed under the Apache License 2.0. See the LICENSE and NOTICE
files distributed alongside this file.

This listing is specific to the wheel named above. The crate graph is resolved
for that wheel's Rust target triple(s), so it describes what this wheel actually
contains: a wheel for a different platform links a different set of crates and
carries its own copy of this file. Where more than one triple is listed the wheel
is a fat binary containing code for each, and the listing covers all of them.

Most of these crates are offered under a choice of licenses, typically "MIT OR
Apache-2.0". Where that is so, the license reproduced below is the one selected for
this distribution.

A few crates vendor third-party code.
For those, the license shown is the one covering what the wheel actually contains, which
may differ from the license the crate's own Cargo manifest declares for its Rust sources.
Clarifications can be read in about.toml in the project's source repository.

The license texts below are grouped by license and by distinct copyright notice.

The NOTICE files that some of these dependencies ship are not reproduced here.
Apache License 2.0 section 4(d) requires those to be relayed in a NOTICE file, so
they appear in the NOTICE distributed alongside this file instead.

